    "title": "Unless / Provided that / As long as",
    "title_ko": "Unless / Provided that / As long as",
    "focus_axis": "grammar"
  },
  "context": {
    "explanation_en": "'Unless' means 'if not': 'I won't go unless you come with me' (= if you don't come). 'Provided that' and 'as long as' mean 'only if', setting a condition for permission or agreement: 'You can borrow it, provided that you return it tomorrow.'",
    "explanation_ko": "'unless'는 '~하지 않는 한'이라는 뜻입니다: 'I won't go unless you come with me'(당신이 안 오면 안 감). 'provided that'과 'as long as'는 '~하기만 하면'이라는 뜻으로, 허락·동의의 조건을 설정합니다: 'You can borrow it, provided that you return it tomorrow.'",
    "key_expressions": [
      {
        "en": "I won't sign unless the terms change.",
        "ko": "조건이 바뀌지 않으면 서명 안 할 거예요."
      },
      {
        "en": "You can stay, provided that you help clean up.",
        "ko": "청소를 도와주기만 하면 있어도 돼요."
      },
      {
        "en": "As long as you're happy, that's all that matters.",
        "ko": "당신이 행복하기만 하면, 그게 다예요."
      }
    ]
  },
